            "text": "In case the studies are conducted in just one member state the protocols and results have to be submitted via national variation in that member state in case of purely national MAs and as EU variation in case of MRP or DCP MAs. In both cases protocols and results have to be submitted as type II variations under C.12 in case the study is not performed as a condition to the MA and as C.9.c in case it concerns a study performed as a condition to the MA falling under Article 21a, 22a or 22 of Directive 2001/83/EC. In case the study results lead to changes in the SmPC a variation type II under C.4 is to be submitted."
